abstract: "Code and saved evaluation records for a study of tuberculosis chest-radiograph classifiers built on frozen RAD-DINO features. Classifiers were developed on Shenzhen, and their validation-selected thresholds were transferred unchanged to Montgomery and a duplicate-screened TBX11K cohort. The archive covers threshold-selection uncertainty, a proposed uncertainty-aware threshold calibration (Neyman-Pearson order-statistic rule), negative-case spectrum, calibration, and secondary encoder and preprocessing comparisons. Scripts regenerate every figure and table of the article from saved per-image scores. Raw radiographs and model binaries are not included."
keywords:
  - tuberculosis
  - chest radiography
  - external validation
  - decision threshold
  - threshold calibration
  - Neyman-Pearson classification
  - calibration
  - reproducibility
